  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Development and demonstration of innovative technologies for value-adding applications of plastic waste from Indian paper mills in rubber and other industries (Paper phase III)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 2019, UNIDO has implemented a project titled #Firm-level demonstration of technologies and productivity enhancement measures for the Indian pulp and paper industry#, wherein innovative technologies for productivity enhancements have been adapted to Indian process conditions and demonstrated through transportable pilot units in paper mills across the country. During implementation, industry stakeholders expressed the need for a viable solution to address the issue of plastic wastes generated in recycled-fibre based mills. UNIDO has undertaken preliminary experiments in collaboration with subject matter experts to explore potential technology options for utilization of plastic waste for application of generated by-products in other industries and energy generation.  The proposed project aims to develop and demonstrate a potential solution to this problem related to disposal/utilization of plastic wastes from paper mills. The objective of the project is to establish a techno-economically viable option for the utilization of plastic wastes generated in recycled fibre-based paper mills through pyrolytic thermochemical conversion and explore value-adding applications in allied industries, such as rubber, for resultant by-products as a way of improving resource efficiency and productivity in target industries. T</narrative>
  </description>
